rsx_live_draw: scissored clears, per-face stencil masks/reference, polygon offset, depth bounds, MRT blend/mask.

For KZ3's stencil-then-cover text (512x512 glyph cache at 0x3A00000) and the deferred renderer:
- CLEAR_SURFACE is limited to the surface clip and the scissor rectangle (ClearRenderTargetView /
  ClearDepthStencilView with one rect), as on RSX (RPCS3 clears the scissor region). An unscissored clear of
  one glyph-cache cell wiped every glyph rendered before it. LD_CLEAR_NO_SCISSOR=1 restores the old clears.
  The z/stencil clear value counts as unwritten by seen[], not by being zero.
- Two-sided stencil: back read/write masks (0x358/0x34C) through D3D12_DEPTH_STENCIL_DESC2 in a pipeline
  state stream and back reference (0x354) through ID3D12GraphicsCommandList8::OMSetFrontAndBackStencilRef,
  when D3D12_OPTIONS14.IndependentFrontAndBackStencilRefMaskSupported; otherwise the front values for both
  faces (logged once). MinGW-w64 14 lacks both declarations; they are declared locally with the SDK layout.
- Polygon offset (fill enable 0xA68, factor 0xA78, units 0xA7C) -> rasterizer SlopeScaledDepthBias/DepthBias.
- Depth bounds (0x380 enable, 0x384/0x388 min/max) -> DEPTH_STENCIL1/2 DepthBoundsTestEnable in the PSO and
  ID3D12GraphicsCommandList1::OMSetDepthBounds per draw, when D3D12_OPTIONS2.DepthBoundsTestSupported.
- Blend colour (SET_BLEND_COLOR 0x31C, BLEND_COLOR2 0x368 for FP16 surfaces) -> OMSetBlendFactor per draw
  (never set before); CONSTANT_ALPHA factors use D3D12_BLEND_ALPHA_FACTOR when D3D12_OPTIONS13 allows.
- LD_RS_LOG lines also print blend factors/equation, blend colour and alpha-test enable.
- MRT: IndependentBlendEnable with the per-target blend enable (0x36C bits 1-3) and colour mask (0x370
  nibbles 1-3); targets 1-3 used to mirror target 0.
All new state is in the PSO key. LD_NO_PSO_STREAM=1 turns the stream path (depth bounds, per-face masks) off.
KZ3 port RSX, 2026-10-08.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.15.0 (SPU pass 81): PR282 z16 clear overlaps, ours kept since 2041 builds the same decode on it (seen-count default, clear rects).

